new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d3af756d85d086976897dca923ac9c39c0a62b5a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Host regression checks
+
+These checks need a C++11 host compiler. The plotting check supplies its own small display stub; no Arduino installation is required. Run from the repository root:
+
+```sh
+c++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -I src tests/data_spline_bounds.cpp -o /tmp/grafici-spline-bounds
+/tmp/grafici-spline-bounds
+c++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -I src tests/numeric_precision.cpp -o /tmp/grafici-numeric-precision
+/tmp/grafici-numeric-precision
+c++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -I tests/support -I src tests/precision_plotting.cpp -o /tmp/grafici-precision-plotting
+/tmp/grafici-precision-plotting
+```
+
+It guards every spline workspace allocation, checks interpolation including the maximum supported source count, injects failure into each allocation, and exercises empty, single-point, zero-output and oversized inputs. Unsupported inputs or allocation failure produce an empty spline (`size() == 0`), whose reads return `INVALID_DATA_VECTOR`. Source count is the minimum of x/y counts and must be between 2 and `N + 1` for the current fixed coefficient arrays.
+
+It also checks that a declared x range extending beyond the supplied knots returns invalid data for an uncovered sample without reading past the source. This does not change interpolation endpoint sampling or validate every numerical precondition, such as strictly increasing knots.
+
+The numeric check validates every binary16 encoding and finite rounding interval, then exercises float/FP16 sources, borrowed casts, ranges, interpolation, splines and projection. The plotting check uses a host drawing-call recorder to instantiate both complete pipelines and check representative pixel endpoints. The recorder does not emulate hardware or rasterization.
+
+For additional host diagnostics, add `-fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer` to the compile command when supported. Keep assertions enabled. Board SRAM/stack measurements remain separate from these host checks.
